# Reverse Proxy HTTP Transport Configuration

The code that builds the reverse proxy transport for `https+insecure://` or `http://` backends is in the `getTransport()` method:

```go
func (rp *reverseProxy) getTransport() *http.Transport {
	return rp.httpTransport.Get(func() *http.Transport {
		maxIdleConnsPerHost, _ := envknob.LookupInt("TS_DEBUG_SERVE_MAX_IDLE_CONNS_PER_HOST")
		dial := rp.lb.dialer.SystemDial
		if rp.socketPath != "" {
			dial = func(ctx context.Context, _, _ string) (net.Conn, error) {
				var d net.Dialer
				return d.DialContext(ctx, "unix", rp.socketPath)
			}
		}

		return &http.Transport{
			DialContext: dial,
			TLSClientConfig: &tls.Config{
				InsecureSkipVerify: rp.insecure,
			},
			ForceAttemptHTTP2:     true,
			MaxIdleConns:          100,
			MaxIdleConnsPerHost:   maxIdleConnsPerHost,
			IdleConnTimeout:       90 * time.Second,
			TLSHandshakeTimeout:   10 * time.Second,
			ExpectContinueTimeout: 1 * time.Second,
		}
	})
}
```

There is no health check or probing of backends when the serve config is set. Backends are only contacted when requests arrive.

